    <content:encoded>Adam is back to contributing to the blog, at least by proxy.

[caption id="attachment_1303" align="aligncenter" width="640"]&lt;a href="http://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/08/wingtips.jpg"&gt;&lt;img class="size-full wp-image-1303" alt="Wingtips" src="http://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/08/wingtips.jpg" width="640" height="480" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Wingtips[/caption]

Just behind Adam's plane (N3989L, with the snazzy red paint job) you can see the wingtip of the business jet. It's a loop of some sort. I've never seen anything like it. Neither had Adam, which is why we have a snap of it.</content:encoded>
